[Music]  welcome back on July 20th Congress will  return to Washington with just one  objective hammering out the next  stimulus bill the bipartisan talks  happening just as the extra $600 in  weekly unemployment benefits is set to  expire at the end of the month joining  me right now is Republican Conference  Chairman senator john barrasso and  senator it's always a pleasure to see  you thank you so much for joining us  tell me what the dreamers are in terms  of the cares after or than the next part  of the cares Act another stimulus plan  yeah there's a consensus we need to do  another bill that'll be in the next  couple of weeks and let me just tell you  what I believe needs to be in it and I  think your viewers will agree number one  it has to focus on getting people back  to work and children back in school  number two it has to focus on saving  lives and to me that means more testing  better treatment and and then of course  a vaccine and finally we need to provide  the liability insurance for our health  care workers for our mom and pops small  businesses and for our schools so they  can all open in a good way now the  Democrats have a proposal already they  passed it a month or so ago and it's  Nancy Pelosi living in handout heaven  it's direct checks to illegal immigrants  it's bailouts to big city and state  pension plans that are run by Democrats  we're not going to do that the focus of  this bill has to be getting people back  to work and paychecks back into their  pockets so so you're back on July 20th  but then there's another recess  beginning on August 8th right do you  think in that three-week period you're  gonna get another stimulus plan passed  and signed before you leave again August  8th well there are a couple of deadlines  as you mentioned one is the enhanced  uninsurance unemployment insurance  benefits that run out on on July 31st  the other is the paycheck protection  program which has been so successful  that runs out on August 8th that's  helped keep about 50 million people on  their you know on a payroll and in  Wyoming we had 13,000 of those loans so  yeah there's a there  an urgency to get this done a lot of  different things in the components of it  the question is should it include  additional relief checks for people who  have still not been able to get back to  work certainly in hard-hit industries  whether it's a service industry the  hospitality industry you know we did  that once before but that was it people  up to $95,000 we're looking at a lower  number there and then the unemployment  insurance is you raised these are  enhanced benefits where they've been  paying people $600 a week above their  own state unemployment benefits right  and some of them are making more to stay  home rather than to go to work stay with  us senator I want to ask you about masks  and whether it should be a policy in  that next act as well we are talking  with Senator bra so we'll be right back  welcome back and we're back with Senator  John Barrasso and Senate I want to ask  you about masks and whether or not that  should be part of your cares Act there  are some states that have made wearing a  mask a policy should it be a national  policy well let me just say Maria as a  doctor I want to congratulate president  Trump for wearing his mask yesterday in  public for the world to see I think that  sends a very strong message to everyone  we know that masks lower the risk of  infection we know it lowers the risk of  death and in this recent uptick I just  think it's even more important than ever  and you know when it comes to opening  schools these are going to be local  decisions state decisions but I just  think in terms of good planning and good  health as people try to resume their  normal lives  masks personal hygiene washing their  hands  socially distancing that's all part of  this as we continue to fight this  disease all right and real quick on the  next cares act when you get back on the  20th it doesn't sound like you're gonna  leave on August 8th without anything  getting done should I assume we will  have another another stimulus package in  that three-week period there is general  agreement we need to work to that end  and we need to deal with the issues  affecting our nation there are still  people who can't go back to work through  no fault of their own because of the  disease because of  medical conditions we need to make sure  that they are cared for but we cannot  continue to pay people more to sit at  home then the go to work and we have so  many help wanted signs around Wyoming  and the country we need to do all we can  to get people back to work and help them  earn that paycheck  senator real quick before we go the  Senate unanimously passed that  bipartisan bill to sanction Chinese  officials who threatened Hong Kong's  Authority but the president hasn't it  signed it yet right what message does  this send to the Communist Party and  will we see this get signed into law do  you think well the Communist Chinese are  not our friends there is no question  about it my message to the Chinese is  never again never again will we as  Americans be dependent upon you the  Communist Chinese for medicines for  materials for minerals what you're  seeing here with what they're doing  mariya with this group with Hong Kong  with their the Chinese incursion into  the South China Sea it's all part of  their big plan to be the military the  economic and the technological  superpower world cannot allow senator  thank you

